// mixed_shape_stillwater_81floaters_bogner_gas.prm
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 81 MIXED FLOATERS (27 spheres + 27 boxes + 27 cylinders) dropped into STILL WATER,
// using the project's own hardcoded reference units (viscosity=0.000214026,
// relaxationRate=1.99743, gravity=7.02618e-06, surfaceTension=0.000849592 -- the
// "useHardcodedUnits true" branch, U=0.02/Re=3100/Fr=1.31/We=15.6188 reference case,
// NOT Bogner's own hardcoded tau=1/1.9/g=7.5e-4 -- see GRAVITY HISTORY below).
//
// GRAVITY HISTORY: the first version of this file used Bogner & Rude (2013)'s raw
// g=7.5e-4 unchanged (job 3922028). It crashed at step 4288/100000 (~5 min in): a
// particle's rotation quaternion went NaN (WALBERLA_CHECK in Quaternion.h:241),
// preceded by a [MEM-WATCH] large-force warning on a particle already sitting on the
// floor (pos z~3). Root cause: Bogner's incompressibility bound (Eq. 10 of
// arXiv:1201.0351, citing Buick & Greated 2000, (lx,ly,lz)*a << cs^2=1/3) is
// satisfied at only a ~9.0% margin in HIS OWN 40-cell-tall domain (40*7.5e-4=0.03),
// but this file kept the full <128,60,180> domain (needed for drop height -- the
// floater grid spans z=64 to z=88) while reusing his g unchanged, giving
// 180*7.5e-4=0.135, a ~40% margin -- nowhere near "<<" cs^2, and unstable in
// practice. A second version rescaled Bogner's gravity to 1.66667e-4 (preserving his
// own 9.0% margin at this domain's height) -- this ran, but was later replaced (this
// version) by switching to true g_SI=9.81: computed for this scenario's actual
// spheres_out.dat/grid scale (dx_SI=3.62694e-4 m, dt_SI=1.15208e-3 s at tau=1.9),
// gravityOverride would need to be 0.0359982 -- checked against Eq. 10 and found to
// violate it by ~19x (180*0.036=6.46 vs the required <<1/3), i.e. guaranteed unstable,
// so it was rejected without running. This file now uses the project's own
// hardcoded-units reference gravity (7.02618e-06) instead of any Bogner or
// true-g_SI value -- weaker than Bogner's rescaled value, so floaters settle even
// more gradually.
//
// GEOMETRY -- reused VERBATIM from the original proven-clean 81-floater "clean-
// factorial" grid (mixed_sed_worked.log, job 3856318, prm=mixed_shape_sedimentation_
// showcase_gas.prm at the time; also mixed_sed2.log job 3854507, 20000-step variant --
// both ran clean). Recovered directly from that log's own config echo (not retyped
// by hand) and cross-checked here: 27+27+27=81. See
// mixed_shape_sedimentation_showcase_pillars_gas.prm's header for the fuller history
// of why the CURRENT mixed_shape_sedimentation_showcase_gas.prm only has 9 floaters
// now (a later 54-floater SCRAMBLED-density variant of this grid crashed; the file
// was reverted to a smaller 3x3 anchor grid rather than restoring the original 81).
// This file restores that original, already-validated 81-floater layout as its own
// showcase, unrelated to that crash investigation.
//
// 9 X-anchors (6/16/26/38/48/58/70/80/90) x 3 Y-replicates (10/30/50) x 3 shapes,
// one sphere+box+cylinder stack per (X,Y). densityRatio constant per stack, set by
// X-anchor block: 6/16/26 -> 0.5, 38/48/58 -> 1.0, 70/80/90 -> 2.0 (the "uniform"
// density arrangement -- proven safe, unlike the scrambled/mixed variants).
// Z fixed per shape: sphere 64, box 76, cylinder 88 (same ~9 LU footprint as each
// shape's own dedicated showcase). No pillars, no flow forcing (still water,
// targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0) -- floaters simply fall from rest and settle by
// buoyancy under the project's own hardcoded-units reference gravity (see GRAVITY
// HISTORY above -- not Bogner's).
//
// BOGNER HARDCODED VALUES -- IMPORTANT CAVEAT: g=7.5e-4 and tau=1/1.9=0.526 are the
// values Bogner & Rude (2013) used ONLY for their single three-cube rotational-
// equilibrium test (Sec. 3.3.1, arXiv:1201.0351) -- a 130x40x40 domain with 3 boxes
// heeled from upright, checking convergence to Fekken-predicted stable angles. Their
// paper does NOT contain any multi-floater/swarm scenario resembling this 81-floater
// grid -- checked directly against the paper's own section list (free-advection
// single-sphere test at a DIFFERENT gravity, g=1e-5, Sec. 3.2.1; floating-cube
// equilibrium at g=7.5e-4, Sec. 3.3.1; nothing else with rigid bodies). There is no
// "similar showcase" in Bogner's own work to validate this specific combination
// (many mixed-shape floaters + his gravity/viscosity) against -- this run applies
// his validated single-object constants to a scenario he never tested, purely to see
// how far mixed-shape multi-floater interactions extrapolate under that regime.
//
// ModelParameters: useBognerThreePhaseMEM + useMemOnlyBuoyancy both true (matching
// every other *_bogner_*_gas.prm file) -- buoyancy support and torque come solely
// from the raw MEM/hydrodynamic force+torque (no separate vSub/cbOff righting-torque
// machinery), matching Bogner's Eq. 18 exactly.
//
// Domain: <128, 60, 180> / cellsPerBlock <32, 20, 30> = 4×3×6 = 72 processes
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 32, 20, 30 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 1, 0 >;   // X and Y periodic — no side walls, only Z floor/ceiling
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             10000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <128, 60, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.862;
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0;       // still water — no flow forcing
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting          false;
   timesteps              100000;
   Re                     3100;
   Fr                     1.31;
   We                     15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits      true;        // project's own fixed reference units (viscosity=0.000214026,
                                       // relaxationRate=1.99743, gravity=7.02618e-06,
                                       // surfaceTension=0.000849592) instead of Bogner's hardcoded
                                       // tau=1/1.9/g=7.5e-4 -- switched off per request; the true
                                       // g_SI=9.81 value for this scenario's grid scale
                                       // (gravityOverride=0.0359982, computed from this domain's
                                       // spheres_out.dat) was checked and violates the LBM
                                       // incompressibility bound (Eq. 10, Buick & Greated 2000:
                                       // domainHeight*g << cs^2=1/3) by ~19x, so it was rejected as
                                       // unusable rather than run.
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.97;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

FloatingSpheres
{
   FloatingSphere { position < 6, 10, 64 >; radius 4.5; densityRatio 0.5; settlingSteps 0; }
   FloatingSphere { position < 6, 30, 64 >; radius 4.5; densityRatio 0.5; settlingSteps 0; }
   FloatingSphere { position < 6, 50, 64 >; radius 4.5; densityRatio 0.5; settlingSteps 0; }
   FloatingSphere { position < 16, 10, 64 >; radius 4.5; densityRatio 0.5; settlingSteps 0; }
